+## Usage reported to `afterModelResponse`
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and is passed the turn's usage summed across every provider call the orchestrator made, so a deployer billing or auditing from the hook counts the tool rounds and not only their last leg ([validated by: sums the usage of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds, not the last round alone](../../src/orchestration/usageReporting.acceptance.test.ts#L59)).
+- A provider that stays silent on some rounds does not poison the total: the rounds that reported are still counted, and a turn in which no provider call reported usage still reports nothing ([validated by: still counts the rounds that reported usage when one reports none, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/usageReporting.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it always reported — the single provider call's usage, unchanged ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
